.TH FL-NETWORK 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-network \- NetworkManager settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-network\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows the network devices managed by NetworkManager with their state,
addresses and speed. Wi-Fi devices list the networks in range with their
signal and security; connect with a password, or to a hidden network.
.PP
\fBAll Connections\fR lists the saved connections: activate, deactivate,
delete, or add a wired, Wi-Fi or VPN connection (\fBAdd\fR). The editor covers the general
settings (name, connect automatically, available to all users), Wi-Fi
(SSID, security, password) and IPv4/IPv6 (automatic, manual or disabled;
addresses, gateway, DNS servers). Changes that need privileges are
authorized through polkit, see \fBfl-polkit-agent\fR(1).
.SS VPN
\fBWireGuard\fR connections are built in: the editor's WireGuard tab has the private key (with
\fBGenerate\fR for a new key pair and the public key to give to the other side), the listen port,
the MTU and the peers (public key, endpoint, allowed IPs, pre-shared key, keepalive); the
addresses and DNS servers are on the IPv4 and IPv6 tabs. \fBImport VPN from File\fR reads
WireGuard \fIwg-quick\fR files (\fI*.conf\fR) and, through the installed NetworkManager VPN
plugins (e.g. network-manager-openvpn), their formats such as \fI.ovpn\fR. For a plugin VPN the
editor shows the user name, password and the plugin's settings as \fIkey = value\fR lines.
.PP
The network indicator of \fBfl-panel\fR(1) opens this program; right-clicking it connects and
disconnects VPNs. The panel asks for the Wi-Fi and VPN passwords that NetworkManager needs (a
secret agent).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBnmcli\fR(1), \fBNetworkManager\fR(8), \fBfl-settings\fR(1)
